{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user has submitted a stitch task (#5152) to modify `cmd/du/main.go` to add traversal control flags. The task title is \"[stitch] cmd/du: depth limit, filesystem boundary, symlinks, and exclusion (srd009-du R2.4-R2.7)\". The four task requirements are:\n   - R1: Implement max depth limit (`-d`/`--max-depth`) per srd009-du R2.4\n   - R2: Implement one-filesystem mode (`-x`/`--one-file-system`) per srd009-du R2.5\n   - R3: Implement dereference mode (`-L`/`--dereference`) per srd009-du R2.6\n   - R4: Implement exclude patterns (`--exclude`) per srd009-du R2.7\n\n   **CRITICAL CONFLICT**: The SRD's actual R2.5-R2.7 are about `-k`, `-m`, and `-c` flags—NOT about `-x`, `-L`, or `--exclude`. Furthermore, the SRD `non_goals` explicitly exclude `--exclude`, `-L/--dereference`, and `-D/--dereference-args`. Per execution constitution E6, features in non_goals must NOT be implemented. The valid work from the SRD is:\n   - R2.4: `-d N`/`--max-depth=N` depth limiting (IN SCOPE)\n   - R2.5: `-k` flag acceptance (IN SCOPE, trivial)\n   - R2.6: `-m` flag for 1M blocks (IN SCOPE)\n   - R2.7: `-c` grand total (ALREADY IMPLEMENTED)\n   - `-x/--one-file-system`: Not in SRD at all (neither goals nor non_goals)\n   - `-L/--dereference`: EXPLICITLY in non_goals — must NOT implement\n   - `--exclude`: EXPLICITLY in non_goals — must NOT implement\n\n   Acceptance criteria: AC1 (build succeeds), AC2 (go vet passes), AC3 (du -d 1 works correctly), AC4 (du -x doesn't cross mount points).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go Unix utils project with differential testing against GNU reference binaries\n   - `pkg/sys.FileInfo` struct with `Dev`, `Ino`, `Blocks`, `Size` fields for filesystem metadata\n   - `pkg/sys.Lstat` fo